 them well you  know what would probably be good for you  is to actually learn some marketing and  sales they go oh I don't want to look  I'm not a Salesman they kind of like  look down it salespeople like it's some  like lower form of human business scum  or something like that and you know you  imagine okay I have to put on a funky  like a weird suit and like a windbreaker  like a car salesman or the sell my  product would never want to do that well  when you really learn sales as I know  you know because your various or your  fantastic sales person that the best  selling methods are consultative selling  where you don't sit down and try to talk  someone into buying you sit down and you  say let me ask you some questions let me  learn about you and find out what all  your problems are and let me see if what  I have is even a fit and then once  you've found out where they're at what  their problems are what all the  challenges they're facing or and what  they'd like to accomplish then you sell  solutions you sell them fixing their  problems you sell them getting what they  want not your thing and the best of the  best of the best salespeople are the  ones that walk in and sit down and ask  much questions and then say my product  can't help you let me refer to some you  know refer you to someone who can  because those are the people that win  the trust and  when they say this is the thing that  will solve your problem the prospects is  that's the thing I need because they're  trustworthy so learning consultative  selling and really learning how to sell  like a professional is very important  know thyself know thyself  this is probably the most famous phrase  handed down from the Greek philosophers  know thyself why is it so important why  is it so profound  and another question why do we do what  we do why do we think the way we think  why do we feel the way we feel why do we  behave in certain patterns and get into  certain relationship patterns in our  lives well these are the magic questions  psychology answers these questions on  the general level but we all have  experiences that are private very  individual and very powerful we have  something that's shaping our thoughts  shaping our emotions shaping our  behavior from the inside why is it so  important to know yourself what does it  mean well I don't think it means to know  what your favorite TV show is or what  your favorite restaurant is I do think  to know yourself means to understand  your personality to understand how  you're wired what you're likely to do in  different situations under different  types of pressure and with different  types of people the reason that it's so  important to know thyself is because  there are many different types of people  in the world and to create success you  must work effectively with yourself and  with others you must know yourself you  must know how you work so you can  control yourself communicate well and  understand what others are communicating  and ultimately increase your  effectiveness communicating and  persuading others and creating the  results that you want in your life it's  also critical to know yourself so you  can understand your weaknesses your soft  spots your Achilles heels and those  things in your life that can hurt you  all of these things are intimately  connected to your personality  understanding your personality is  understanding yourself if you'd like to  know thyself then know thy personality  in the past the paradigm that we use as  business owners and marketers is that we  have some entry-level stuff that we use  to get prospects attention and those  things might be like advertisements or  we might offer you know some free  information or a free report or  sometimes even pre-recorded messages or  free consultations and then we move and  we have the kind of mid-level priced  products that we sell and upsell to and  then we have our highest end products  that we sell to our best customers well  what's happening now and what's  happening a lot and accelerating over  the last few years with the rise of the  Internet  is more and more stuff is available for  free there are more companies that are  funded by venture capital that have 50  million dollars in cash in the bank that  they don't know what to do with so  they're just giving stuff away to  customers things are becoming cheaper  and cheaper to produce and all that  stuff that you used to think of as being  your your real valuable stuff now you've  got your competitors giving it away to  your customers so if you can't beat them  you need to join them and in fact what I  think you need to do is get in front of  them and what we do is we take that line  that was the stuff that we used to give  away for free and we move it deeper into  the customer relationship and the things  that we used to charge money for are  entry-level products now we give away  and what that does is it builds  relationships with more customers it  allows us to kind of widen our funnel so  to speak and attract a lot more  prospects so let me give you an example  from one of our current businesses as I  mentioned before we have a company  called double your dating and in that  company we teach dating advice to men  now we actually have another company  that we teach dating advice to women and  we have others that we teach other kind  of self-help and personal development  topics but the one that started it all  was the company called double your  dating and when I originally sat down to  work on the marketing for that that  company I started playing around with  email newsletters and at first the  newsletters that I sent out were very  short and there were excerpts of some of  our products and other stuff that wasn't  really all that valuable but it was free  and I thought that people would you know  kind of find it find some value in it we  started sending them out well as we  developed I started writing longer and  longer newsletters and I realized that  the more valuable the newsletter the  more it caused people to want to invest  in our products and at one point I said  to myself you know what I want to create  the most valuable newsletter that has  ever been created on any topic ever in  history and then I want to give it away  I set the bar very high  and when I was thinking this I was  thinking about financial newsletters  that sometimes cost thousands of dollars  a year I mean I was really put in the  bar up there and if you've ever read  some of our newsletters you'll see that  they average probably fifteen or twenty  pages long and we send them out every  couple  days some of them are as long as 30 or  40 pages of value jam-packed with  entertaining useful step-by-step  mindsets everything you could possibly  need and we get letters from all around  the world constantly talking about how  the appreciation thanking us for the  value that we jam-pack in these  newsletters if you subscribe to that  newsletter and you're interested in  getting dating advice you will have your  picture filled up to the brim I  recommend that you ask yourself how can  you move the free line in your business  you might not want to go overboard like  we did but what's an entry level product  that doesn't cost you much to produce  that you can just give away to your  customers if you don't use information  products in your business things like  email newsletters and downloadable  ebooks and CD and DVD courses and  streaming video like you're watching  right now then you really need to do  that and you need to learn about it as  soon as you possibly can the idea of  bringing light to failures right and you  mentioned that in our business we try to  encourage people as soon as you see  something that goes wrong or you screw  something up raise your hand it's a half  screwed-up or I see something that's  wrong over here and make it a win and I  just want to just slip this in there a  reason why that's so important is that  we humans don't like to look bad in  front of others we don't like to look  like idiots we don't like to screw screw  things up so what we do in a business or  a corporate environment is we screw  something up and then we take it and we  hide it and we isolate we try to not let  anyone see it  we try to go to work fixing it  unfortunately if you've screwed  something up it probably means that you  didn't know how to do it right the first  time and it probably also means further  that if you take it and isolate and try  to fix it you're probably can even make  it worse and if you let people have that  mentality of you're going to get in  trouble if you screw something up  they're going to isolate they're going  to go try to fix it they're going to  make it worse  and then when they show up and it gets  discovered they might try to use a  scapegoat and say it wasn't my fault or  someone else did it and you know it's  just a really bad situation so if you  can make an environment or culture we're  finding screw-ups raising your hand when  something goes wrong  saying I made a mistake is a win and the  person to spot the screw-up  the fastest is the biggest winner then I  think you can move forward very quickly  and you can as W Edwards Deming said you  can drive out fear which is one of the  most important things you can do in an  organization thank you so much for  watching I made this video because  Corpus forte asked me to so if there's a  famous entrepreneur that you want me to  profile next leave it in the comments  below and I'll see what I can do  I'd also love to know which if Evan  pagans top 10 rules hit you the hardest  leave it in the comments and I'll join  in the discussion thank you so much for  watching  continue to believe and I'll see you  soon
 

